    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22792" root="شك" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِكَاكٌ</span></b>  <i>Tents arranged in a row:</i> (O, K:) one
says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَرَبُوا بُيُوتَهُمْ شِكَاكًا</span> <i>They pitched their tents
in one row:</i> but accord. to Th, it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِكَاكًا</span>, [q. v.],
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السِّكَّةُ</span>. (TA.)

